   "importance": 4,
   "certainty": "reconstructed",
   "summary": "When the old river harbour by the Forum Boarium grew too small, the aediles M. Aemilius Lepidus and L. Aemilius Paullus laid out a new Emporium on the open plain south of the Aventine in 193 BC, about 500 m of river front.",
